1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,912
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:02,912 --> 00:00:04,167
Alright!

3
00:00:04,167 --> 00:00:06,167
We're exploring Tokyo today!

4
00:00:06,426 --> 00:00:09,463
Look at this!

5
00:00:09,716 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Kaminarimon Gate & Nakamise Street in Asakusa

6
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:14,474
Ah, here we are!

7
00:00:14,497 --> 00:00:17,330
Good morning!

8
00:00:17,353 --> 00:00:20,136
Good morning!

9
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,960
Sorry I'm late.

10
00:00:22,983 --> 00:00:25,817
No worries!

11
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:29,540
This is Kaminarimon Gate.

12
00:00:29,562 --> 00:00:33,159
That lantern is huge!

13
00:00:33,182 --> 00:00:36,149
Wow, so many people!

14
00:00:36,172 --> 00:00:40,310
Yeah, it's a famous spot.

15
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:43,567
Can I take a photo?

16
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:46,223
Sure, go ahead!

17
00:00:46,246 --> 00:00:48,679
I'll take it for you.

18
00:00:48,702 --> 00:00:51,136
Thanks a lot!

19
00:00:51,159 --> 00:00:55,464
Look at all those shops over there!

20
00:00:55,487 --> 00:00:59,254
Yep, that's Nakamise Street.

21
00:00:59,277 --> 00:01:01,586
Let's go!

22
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:04,796
Mmm, something smells sweet.

23
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:07,366
What's this?

24
00:01:07,389 --> 00:01:10,266
It's Ningyo-yaki.

25
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:15,157
It's filled with sweet red bean paste.

26
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,813
That looks delicious!

27
00:01:17,836 --> 00:01:20,744
I want to buy some.

28
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:23,639
Let's get some then!

29
00:01:23,662 --> 00:01:26,401
I'll get some too.

30
00:01:26,424 --> 00:01:28,958
Ooh, it's hot!

31
00:01:28,981 --> 00:01:32,481
Should we eat while we walk?

32
00:01:32,504 --> 00:01:36,737
Oh, we shouldn't eat while walking here.

33
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:39,478
Why not?

34
00:01:39,501 --> 00:01:44,808
It's crowded, so it's dangerous.

35
00:01:44,832 --> 00:01:46,732
Got it.

36
00:01:46,755 --> 00:01:49,754
Let's eat in front of the shop.

37
00:01:49,778 --> 00:01:51,746
Good idea.

38
00:01:51,770 --> 00:01:55,803
It's so sweet and tasty!

39
00:01:55,826 --> 00:01:59,393
Yeah, I could go for some tea now.

40
00:01:59,415 --> 00:02:03,649
There's a vending machine over there!

41
00:02:03,672 --> 00:02:06,105
Perfect!

42
00:02:06,128 --> 00:02:09,495
Alright, let's head to the temple.

43
00:02:09,518 --> 00:02:14,789
Sure! That's the main hall of Senso-ji over there.

44
00:02:14,812 --> 00:02:17,879
That building is massive!

45
00:02:17,902 --> 00:02:20,420
What do we do here?

46
00:02:20,443 --> 00:02:24,477
First, we wash our hands over there.

47
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,886
The water's cold!

48
00:02:27,910 --> 00:02:30,743
What's next?

49
00:02:30,766 --> 00:02:34,540
We offer some money and make a wish.

50
00:02:34,563 --> 00:02:36,909
Got it.

51
00:02:36,932 --> 00:02:39,681
What are you going to wish for?

52
00:02:39,705 --> 00:02:42,172
It's a secret.

53
00:02:42,195 --> 00:02:46,061
Oh, would you like to draw an omikuji fortune slip?

54
00:02:46,084 --> 00:02:48,951
What's an omikuji?

55
00:02:48,974 --> 00:02:53,141
It's a slip of paper with your fortune written on it.

56
00:02:53,165 --> 00:02:55,798
It's 100 yen.

57
00:02:55,821 --> 00:02:58,288
That sounds fun!

58
00:02:58,311 --> 00:03:00,420
I'll draw one.

59
00:03:00,444 --> 00:03:03,382
Shake the box.

60
00:03:03,405 --> 00:03:06,272
A number will come out.

61
00:03:06,295 --> 00:03:08,961
It's number 35.

62
00:03:08,984 --> 00:03:10,953
This one?

63
00:03:10,977 --> 00:03:15,844
Yes, open that drawer, please.

64
00:03:15,868 --> 00:03:18,368
There's a slip of paper inside.

65
00:03:18,391 --> 00:03:21,224
What does it say?

66
00:03:21,247 --> 00:03:24,590
It says 'Daikichi'—great blessing!

67
00:03:24,613 --> 00:03:28,183
That's the best fortune you can get!

68
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:30,378
Really?

69
00:03:30,401 --> 00:03:33,312
I'm so happy!

70
00:03:33,336 --> 00:03:36,208
Mine is 'Kichi'—good luck.

71
00:03:36,232 --> 00:03:38,732
That's great too!

72
00:03:38,755 --> 00:03:42,488
Japanese culture is so much fun!

73
00:03:42,511 --> 00:03:51,520
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

74
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,020
Scene 2: Meeting Up Tips – How to Find Each Other Easily

75
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:57,287
Hello? Where are you now?

76
00:03:57,309 --> 00:04:00,694
I'm in front of the station.

77
00:04:00,718 --> 00:04:04,384
I don't see the dog statue.

78
00:04:04,407 --> 00:04:08,707
The dog statue is Hachiko, right?

79
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:12,605
I'm there right now.

80
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:17,662
There are too many people—I can't see you at all!

81
00:04:17,685 --> 00:04:21,918
What do you see from where you are?

82
00:04:21,941 --> 00:04:26,208
I see a green train.

83
00:04:26,231 --> 00:04:30,597
That's on the opposite side of Hachiko.

84
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:33,459
Come this way.

85
00:04:33,483 --> 00:04:36,583
Got it.

86
00:04:36,606 --> 00:04:39,878
Wait just a moment.

87
00:04:39,902 --> 00:04:43,009
Oh, I see you now!

88
00:04:43,032 --> 00:04:45,866
Over here!

89
00:04:45,888 --> 00:04:48,222
Sorry about that.

90
00:04:48,245 --> 00:04:51,952
There were so many people—I got lost.

91
00:04:51,975 --> 00:04:56,409
Shibuya is always crowded.

92
00:04:56,432 --> 00:05:00,565
Is this the famous Hachiko statue?

93
00:05:00,588 --> 00:05:03,121
Yes, it is.

94
00:05:03,144 --> 00:05:08,451
Hachiko waited here every day for his owner.

95
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:12,242
That's such a famous story!

96
00:05:12,266 --> 00:05:17,166
Alright, let's cross at that intersection.

97
00:05:17,189 --> 00:05:22,561
Wow, so many people are walking!

98
00:05:22,585 --> 00:05:26,152
This is the famous Shibuya Scramble Crossing.

99
00:05:26,175 --> 00:05:28,764
Be careful.

100
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:32,965
No one's bumping into each other—amazing!

101
00:05:32,989 --> 00:05:35,456
That's incredible!

102
00:05:35,479 --> 00:05:38,277
It really is!

103
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:41,800
Shall we take a little break?

104
00:05:41,823 --> 00:05:44,256
Yes, it is.

105
00:05:44,279 --> 00:05:47,779
Let's go to that café over there.

106
00:05:47,802 --> 00:05:52,436
There's an empty seat by the window on the second floor.

107
00:05:52,459 --> 00:05:56,532
You can see the intersection really well from here.

108
00:05:56,555 --> 00:05:58,947
That's interesting.

109
00:05:58,970 --> 00:06:02,604
Let's order some drinks.

110
00:06:02,627 --> 00:06:06,160
What would you like?

111
00:06:06,183 --> 00:06:11,153
I'll have a small iced coffee, please.

112
00:06:11,177 --> 00:06:14,843
I'll go for a medium.

113
00:06:14,866 --> 00:06:19,700
Japan's small sizes are a bit tiny, aren't they?

114
00:06:19,723 --> 00:06:23,641
Is it different in your country?

115
00:06:23,665 --> 00:06:25,984
Yes, it is.

116
00:06:26,007 --> 00:06:30,178
The sizes are bigger in my country.

117
00:06:30,201 --> 00:06:36,834
So, a medium in my country is like a small in yours?

118
00:06:36,857 --> 00:06:39,642
I think so.

119
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:43,445
The prices are a bit higher too.

120
00:06:43,469 --> 00:06:46,102
Really?

121
00:06:46,125 --> 00:06:50,192
Café prices are a bit steep, huh?

122
00:06:50,215 --> 00:06:55,515
But the view makes it worth it.

123
00:06:55,538 --> 00:06:57,731
Yes, it is.

124
00:06:57,754 --> 00:07:01,034
The coffee is delicious too.

125
00:07:01,057 --> 00:07:04,966
Where should we go after this?

126
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:09,137
There are so many clothing stores around here.

127
00:07:09,161 --> 00:07:12,136
Shall we check them out?

128
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,060
I'd love to!

129
00:07:15,083 --> 00:07:17,516
I'm excited!

130
00:07:17,539 --> 00:07:24,644
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment! *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

131
00:07:24,644 --> 00:07:26,144
Scene 3: Shopping for Figures in Akihabara

132
00:07:26,144 --> 00:07:29,844
We've arrived in Akihabara!

133
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:34,000
There are so many anime billboards!

134
00:07:34,024 --> 00:07:38,809
Yep, it's the city of electronics and anime.

135
00:07:38,832 --> 00:07:42,870
There are so many unique buildings here.

136
00:07:42,894 --> 00:07:46,561
Are we going shopping today?

137
00:07:46,584 --> 00:07:51,337
Yes, I want to get an anime figure.

138
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:54,515
What kind of anime do you like?

139
00:07:54,539 --> 00:07:59,126
I love anime with ninjas and samurais.

140
00:07:59,149 --> 00:08:02,289
Those are really popular!

141
00:08:02,313 --> 00:08:05,846
Let's go to a big store.

142
00:08:05,869 --> 00:08:11,302
Wow, there are so many items on display!

143
00:08:11,325 --> 00:08:14,894
They have toys and games too!

144
00:08:14,918 --> 00:08:18,856
Oh, I found the figure I was looking for!

145
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:21,713
That's great!

146
00:08:21,736 --> 00:08:24,281
How much is it?

147
00:08:24,304 --> 00:08:27,888
There's no price tag.

148
00:08:27,912 --> 00:08:31,812
It's inside the display case.

149
00:08:31,835 --> 00:08:34,968
Let's ask the staff.

150
00:08:34,991 --> 00:08:40,091
Excuse me, could you show me this one?

151
00:08:40,114 --> 00:08:43,747
The staff member took it out for us.

152
00:08:43,770 --> 00:08:46,670
It looks so cool!

153
00:08:46,693 --> 00:08:49,031
How much is it?

154
00:08:49,054 --> 00:08:53,088
They said it's 4,000 yen.

155
00:08:53,111 --> 00:08:55,267
What do you think?

156
00:08:55,290 --> 00:08:58,646
It's a bit pricey, isn't it?

157
00:08:58,670 --> 00:09:02,403
Do you have a smaller size?

158
00:09:02,426 --> 00:09:06,936
We have smaller sizes on the other shelf.

159
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,594
How much is that?

160
00:09:09,618 --> 00:09:12,684
It's 1,500 yen.

161
00:09:12,707 --> 00:09:15,007
This one?

162
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:19,982
Yes, I'd like that one in blue.

163
00:09:20,006 --> 00:09:23,706
We don’t have it in blue, I’m afraid.

164
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:26,562
We only have it in red.

165
00:09:26,585 --> 00:09:29,052
Really?

166
00:09:29,076 --> 00:09:32,709
Okay, I’ll take the red one then.

167
00:09:32,732 --> 00:09:35,769
Are you buying it as a souvenir?

168
00:09:35,793 --> 00:09:40,228
No, I’m going to decorate my room with it.

169
00:09:40,251 --> 00:09:42,619
That sounds nice!

170
00:09:42,643 --> 00:09:46,743
There’s a gacha machine over there, by the way.

171
00:09:46,766 --> 00:09:50,479
What kind of machine is that?

172
00:09:50,502 --> 00:09:55,082
You put in money, turn the knob, and a toy comes out.

173
00:09:55,106 --> 00:09:59,461
That sounds fun! I’ll give it a try.

174
00:09:59,484 --> 00:10:02,664
Please insert 300 yen.

175
00:10:02,688 --> 00:10:06,721
Oh, a cute cat came out!

176
00:10:06,744 --> 00:10:10,411
That’s a keychain.

177
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:14,778
I’ll attach it to my bag. I’m so happy!

178
00:10:14,802 --> 00:10:16,302
Scene 4: Takeshita Street in Harajuku / Exploring the Famous Takeshita Street

179
00:10:16,302 --> 00:10:20,268
Harajuku is so crowded, isn’t it?

180
00:10:20,291 --> 00:10:24,996
There are so many people wearing cute outfits.

181
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:28,186
This is Takeshita Street.

182
00:10:28,209 --> 00:10:31,158
It’s a famous street.

183
00:10:31,182 --> 00:10:34,654
There’s a shop over there.

184
00:10:34,677 --> 00:10:37,344
Can I take a look?

185
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:40,234
Sure, go ahead!

186
00:10:40,256 --> 00:10:42,445
Let’s go in.

187
00:10:42,469 --> 00:10:47,102
This T-shirt is so cute!

188
00:10:47,125 --> 00:10:50,263
The colors are beautiful, aren’t they?

189
00:10:50,287 --> 00:10:53,204
I think it’ll look great on you.

190
00:10:53,227 --> 00:10:56,461
Can I try it on?

191
00:10:56,484 --> 00:10:59,184
Go ahead.

192
00:10:59,207 --> 00:11:01,274
I’ll wait here.

193
00:11:01,297 --> 00:11:03,830
How does it look?

194
00:11:03,853 --> 00:11:06,520
Does it look weird?

195
00:11:06,543 --> 00:11:10,976
No, the size is just right.

196
00:11:10,999 --> 00:11:14,232
Okay, I’ll take this one.

197
00:11:14,255 --> 00:11:18,432
Shall we grab something sweet next?

198
00:11:18,456 --> 00:11:21,189
I’m all for it!

199
00:11:21,212 --> 00:11:23,512
What would you like?

200
00:11:23,535 --> 00:11:27,974
Harajuku is famous for its crepes.

201
00:11:27,998 --> 00:11:30,465
I’d love to try one.

202
00:11:30,488 --> 00:11:32,922
Where should we buy it?

203
00:11:32,945 --> 00:11:36,820
There’s a shop just around that corner.

204
00:11:36,844 --> 00:11:40,610
There are so many flavors to choose from!

205
00:11:40,633 --> 00:11:42,993
I can’t decide!

206
00:11:43,016 --> 00:11:47,583
I’ll go for the strawberry and banana crepe.

207
00:11:47,606 --> 00:11:52,549
I’ll have the chocolate and ice cream one.

208
00:11:52,572 --> 00:11:56,079
It’s sweet and delicious!

209
00:11:56,103 --> 00:12:00,136
Yes, it’s really good!

210
00:12:00,159 --> 00:12:04,136
Alright, let’s walk around a bit more.

211
00:12:04,159 --> 00:12:06,865
Where are we heading?

212
00:12:06,889 --> 00:12:11,475
Meiji Jingu, a serene shrine.

213
00:12:11,499 --> 00:12:14,071
Is it nearby?

214
00:12:14,095 --> 00:12:18,228
Yes, it's right behind the station.

215
00:12:18,251 --> 00:12:22,396
There are so many tall trees!

216
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:26,986
It's completely different from the street we were on earlier.

217
00:12:27,009 --> 00:12:31,127
It's so peaceful and cool here.

218
00:12:31,151 --> 00:12:36,864
I can hear birds chirping.

219
00:12:36,888 --> 00:12:39,721
It's like a forest in the heart of Tokyo.

220
00:12:39,744 --> 00:12:44,127
I love this quiet place.

221
00:12:44,150 --> 00:12:47,017
Me too.

222
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:50,173
It really calms the mind.

223
00:12:50,196 --> 00:12:51,696
Scene 5: Exploring Tokyo Tower

224
00:12:51,696 --> 00:12:54,811
There it is!

225
00:12:54,835 --> 00:12:58,514
That's Tokyo Tower.

226
00:12:58,537 --> 00:13:03,837
Wow, it's so big and red!

227
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:09,493
It looks really tall from down here.

228
00:13:09,516 --> 00:13:13,183
I can't wait to go up!

229
00:13:13,206 --> 00:13:17,758
Let's buy tickets over there.

230
00:13:17,782 --> 00:13:20,415
How much is it?

231
00:13:20,438 --> 00:13:25,338
It's 1,200 yen for one adult.

232
00:13:25,361 --> 00:13:29,194
I'll pay for both of us.

233
00:13:29,217 --> 00:13:31,595
Thanks a lot!

234
00:13:31,619 --> 00:13:35,119
That's 2,400 yen.

235
00:13:35,142 --> 00:13:39,775
Shall we take the elevator up?

236
00:13:39,798 --> 00:13:41,746
Yes, it is.

237
00:13:41,770 --> 00:13:45,603
We'll have to wait a bit for the observation deck.

238
00:13:45,626 --> 00:13:49,660
There are so many people in line.

239
00:13:49,683 --> 00:13:53,185
Look at the view outside!

240
00:13:53,208 --> 00:13:56,475
We're going higher and higher.

241
00:13:56,498 --> 00:13:59,414
It's a little scary.

242
00:13:59,438 --> 00:14:02,871
We've arrived at the observation deck.

243
00:14:02,894 --> 00:14:05,400
Let's get off.

244
00:14:05,423 --> 00:14:10,890
Wow, you can see all of Tokyo from here!

245
00:14:10,913 --> 00:14:15,413
There's a tall tower over there.

246
00:14:15,436 --> 00:14:18,303
Is that Skytree?

247
00:14:18,326 --> 00:14:22,294
Yes, that's right.

248
00:14:22,317 --> 00:14:25,984
You can see the ocean from here.

249
00:14:26,006 --> 00:14:29,440
There are boats sailing.

250
00:14:29,463 --> 00:14:31,765
It's beautiful.

251
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:37,167
Since the weather's nice, we might be able to see Mt. Fuji.

252
00:14:37,191 --> 00:14:39,658
Where is it?

253
00:14:39,681 --> 00:14:42,039
I want to see it!

254
00:14:42,062 --> 00:14:45,813
It's that distant mountain over there.

255
00:14:45,837 --> 00:14:48,187
Can you see it?

256
00:14:48,210 --> 00:14:54,164
Hmm, there are some clouds, so I can't see it.

257
00:14:54,188 --> 00:14:57,088
That's too bad.

258
00:14:57,111 --> 00:15:00,746
Oh, come over here!

259
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:03,942
What is it?

260
00:15:03,965 --> 00:15:07,399
The floor is made of glass!

261
00:15:07,422 --> 00:15:11,923
Yes, you can see right through to the ground below.

262
00:15:11,946 --> 00:15:14,413
Try standing on it.

263
00:15:14,437 --> 00:15:17,023
No way!

264
00:15:17,047 --> 00:15:19,913
It's really scary.

265
00:15:19,936 --> 00:15:23,003
No worries!

266
00:15:23,026 --> 00:15:26,207
It's absolutely unbreakable.

267
00:15:26,230 --> 00:15:29,330
I'll just ride for a bit.

268
00:15:29,353 --> 00:15:34,111
Wow, this car is so small!

269
00:15:34,135 --> 00:15:37,035
It's fun, isn't it?

270
00:15:37,058 --> 00:15:40,043
Let's take a photo.

271
00:15:40,066 --> 00:15:44,533
Yes. My legs are shaking.

272
00:15:44,556 --> 00:15:49,723
Shall we look at some souvenirs before we head back?

273
00:15:49,746 --> 00:15:53,926
I want some tower-shaped sweets.

274
00:15:53,949 --> 00:15:57,916
There are lots of shops downstairs.

275
00:15:57,939 --> 00:16:01,726
I want to buy a lot for my family.

276
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:03,909
Let's go!

277
00:16:03,933 --> 00:16:05,433
Scene 6: Stunning Views of Shinjuku and Mt. Fuji

278
00:16:05,433 --> 00:16:08,615
We've arrived in Shinjuku.

279
00:16:08,638 --> 00:16:12,421
There are so many tall buildings here.

280
00:16:12,445 --> 00:16:17,017
Yes, that's the Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building.

281
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:19,774
It's huge!

282
00:16:19,797 --> 00:16:23,510
There's a free observation deck.

283
00:16:23,533 --> 00:16:26,209
Let's go!

284
00:16:26,233 --> 00:16:30,366
Yes, the elevator is really fast.

285
00:16:30,389 --> 00:16:32,770
We're here.

286
00:16:32,794 --> 00:16:36,094
The view is amazing!

287
00:16:36,117 --> 00:16:39,884
Yeah. What's that mountain over there?

288
00:16:39,907 --> 00:16:42,773
That's Mt. Fuji.

289
00:16:42,796 --> 00:16:47,552
The weather's great today, so it's really clear.

290
00:16:47,576 --> 00:16:50,843
Can I take a photo?

291
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:53,257
Sure, go ahead!

292
00:16:53,281 --> 00:16:56,114
Shall I take a photo for you?

293
00:16:56,137 --> 00:16:58,437
Yes, please.

294
00:16:58,460 --> 00:17:02,193
Alright, say cheese!

295
00:17:02,216 --> 00:17:04,411
Thanks a lot!

296
00:17:04,434 --> 00:17:09,203
Next, let's head to Shinjuku Gyoen.

297
00:17:09,227 --> 00:17:12,360
What's Shinjuku Gyoen?

298
00:17:12,383 --> 00:17:15,483
It's a huge park.

299
00:17:15,506 --> 00:17:18,273
It's really spacious.

300
00:17:18,296 --> 00:17:21,008
Is it close to the station?

301
00:17:21,031 --> 00:17:24,664
It's about a 15-minute walk.

302
00:17:24,687 --> 00:17:27,025
Got it.

303
00:17:27,049 --> 00:17:29,283
Let's go!

304
00:17:29,306 --> 00:17:32,214
This is the entrance.

305
00:17:32,237 --> 00:17:35,003
Please buy a ticket.

306
00:17:35,026 --> 00:17:37,728
How much is it?

307
00:17:37,751 --> 00:17:41,885
It's 500 yen for one adult.

308
00:17:41,908 --> 00:17:43,886
Got it.

309
00:17:43,910 --> 00:17:46,707
Let's go inside.

310
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:50,697
Wow, there's so much greenery!

311
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:53,420
It really is!

312
00:17:53,443 --> 00:17:56,025
It's so peaceful.

313
00:17:56,048 --> 00:18:00,553
Shall we have lunch on that bench over there?

314
00:18:00,577 --> 00:18:02,844
That sounds nice!

315
00:18:02,867 --> 00:18:05,866
I've already bought a bento.

316
00:18:05,890 --> 00:18:09,403
Oh, there are crows!

317
00:18:09,427 --> 00:18:12,618
Those crows are huge!

318
00:18:12,641 --> 00:18:16,608
Crows will eat your bento.

319
00:18:16,631 --> 00:18:18,664
That's dangerous!

320
00:18:18,687 --> 00:18:22,664
Then let's go under that tree over there.

321
00:18:22,687 --> 00:18:25,387
Let's do that.

322
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:28,196
This spot is safe.

323
00:18:28,219 --> 00:18:30,886
Let's eat our bento.

324
00:18:30,909 --> 00:18:33,542
This is delicious!

325
00:18:33,565 --> 00:18:35,674
Yes, it is.

326
00:18:35,698 --> 00:18:41,132
Shinjuku is an exciting city with towering buildings and lush parks.

327
00:18:41,155 --> 00:18:42,655
Scene 7: Exploring Ueno Park – A Wildlife Adventure

328
00:18:42,655 --> 00:18:47,021
This is Ueno Park.

329
00:18:47,044 --> 00:18:50,278
Wow, there are so many people here!

330
00:18:50,301 --> 00:18:54,934
Yeah. Let’s head to the zoo.

331
00:18:54,957 --> 00:18:57,857
I really want to see the pandas.

332
00:18:57,881 --> 00:19:01,625
Look, there’s a panda over there!

333
00:19:01,648 --> 00:19:06,281
Oh no, the line is huge!

334
00:19:06,304 --> 00:19:09,971
I heard the wait is 60 minutes.

335
00:19:09,994 --> 00:19:12,861
An hour?

336
00:19:12,885 --> 00:19:15,597
That’s a long time.

337
00:19:15,621 --> 00:19:19,054
Should we see the pandas later?

338
00:19:19,077 --> 00:19:21,580
Good idea.

339
00:19:21,603 --> 00:19:25,536
Let’s check out the elephants first.

340
00:19:25,559 --> 00:19:28,493
The elephants are over there.

341
00:19:28,516 --> 00:19:32,649
They’re so big and majestic!

342
00:19:32,672 --> 00:19:38,139
Hey, the panda line is shorter now!

343
00:19:38,162 --> 00:19:40,228
Let's go!

344
00:19:40,251 --> 00:19:43,234
Aww, the panda is sleeping.

345
00:19:43,258 --> 00:19:46,358
So cute!

346
00:19:46,381 --> 00:19:49,937
I got so many great photos!

347
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:54,327
Next, let’s head to Ameya-Yokocho.

348
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:57,461
What’s Ameya-Yokocho?

349
00:19:57,485 --> 00:20:01,418
It’s a bustling shopping district.

350
00:20:01,441 --> 00:20:04,974
You can find all sorts of great deals there.

351
00:20:04,997 --> 00:20:08,064
I want to do some shopping!

352
00:20:08,087 --> 00:20:10,954
Let’s walk there.

353
00:20:10,977 --> 00:20:13,556
It’s really close.

354
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:17,113
There are so many shops!

355
00:20:17,137 --> 00:20:21,270
Look, they have fresh fish and fruit!

356
00:20:21,293 --> 00:20:24,793
There are also stores selling clothes and shoes.

357
00:20:24,816 --> 00:20:28,731
Oh, I want those shoes!

358
00:20:28,754 --> 00:20:31,221
How much is it?

359
00:20:31,244 --> 00:20:34,279
They’re 5,000 yen.

360
00:20:34,303 --> 00:20:37,210
That’s a bit expensive.

361
00:20:37,233 --> 00:20:40,700
Let’s ask the shopkeeper if they can lower the price.

362
00:20:40,723 --> 00:20:43,223
Sorry about that.

363
00:20:43,246 --> 00:20:47,346
Could you lower the price on these shoes, please?

364
00:20:47,369 --> 00:20:52,835
The shopkeeper says 4,000 yen is fine!

365
00:20:52,858 --> 00:20:55,292
That’s great!

366
00:20:55,315 --> 00:20:57,348
I’ll take them.

367
00:20:57,371 --> 00:20:59,874
Nice!

368
00:20:59,898 --> 00:21:04,294
Next, let’s buy some fruit and try it!

369
00:21:04,317 --> 00:21:05,817
Scene 8: Buying Train Tickets – A Quick Guide

370
00:21:05,817 --> 00:21:09,522
We’re taking the Yurikamome Line.

371
00:21:09,545 --> 00:21:12,534
Is this the Yurikamome?

372
00:21:12,557 --> 00:21:16,791
Yes, it looks like a monorail.

373
00:21:16,814 --> 00:21:20,047
Where do we buy tickets?

374
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:23,437
We can buy them at that machine over there.

375
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:27,893
How much is it to Odaiba Kaihin Koen?

376
00:21:27,916 --> 00:21:31,313
It’s 330 yen.

377
00:21:31,336 --> 00:21:34,528
Do they accept IC cards?

378
00:21:34,552 --> 00:21:37,586
Yes, I have one.

379
00:21:37,609 --> 00:21:41,523
Great, let’s use the card to enter.

380
00:21:41,546 --> 00:21:45,613
Oh, it won't go in.

381
00:21:45,636 --> 00:21:49,349
Maybe I don't have enough money.

382
00:21:49,372 --> 00:21:52,539
What should I do?

383
00:21:52,562 --> 00:21:57,062
Please add money at that machine over there.

384
00:21:57,085 --> 00:21:59,785
I'll add 1,000 yen.

385
00:21:59,808 --> 00:22:02,943
Okay, I've added it.

386
00:22:02,967 --> 00:22:05,300
Let's get on.

387
00:22:05,323 --> 00:22:08,996
The front seat is empty.

388
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:11,374
Let's sit down.

389
00:22:11,397 --> 00:22:14,497
The view is amazing!

390
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:18,087
You can see Rainbow Bridge.

391
00:22:18,110 --> 00:22:21,143
The ocean looks so beautiful.

392
00:22:21,166 --> 00:22:25,633
Alright, we've arrived at Odaiba.

393
00:22:25,656 --> 00:22:29,289
There's the Statue of Liberty!

394
00:22:29,312 --> 00:22:32,746
Shall we take a commemorative photo?

395
00:22:32,768 --> 00:22:35,355
I'd love a photo of the two of us.

396
00:22:35,378 --> 00:22:38,878
Let's ask that person.

397
00:22:38,901 --> 00:22:42,635
Excuse me, could you take our picture, please?

398
00:22:42,659 --> 00:22:46,125
Alright, say cheese!

399
00:22:46,149 --> 00:22:48,668
Thank you so much!

400
00:22:48,691 --> 00:22:51,457
It turned out great!

401
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:54,047
That's great!

402
00:22:54,070 --> 00:22:57,252
Want to take a walk by the sea?

403
00:22:57,275 --> 00:23:00,575
There's a sandy beach here.

404
00:23:00,598 --> 00:23:03,831
The water feels cold.

405
00:23:03,854 --> 00:23:07,426
In the summer, this place gets really crowded.

406
00:23:07,450 --> 00:23:11,816
There's a huge shopping mall over there.

407
00:23:11,839 --> 00:23:14,739
Let's go inside.

408
00:23:14,762 --> 00:23:17,317
It's nice and cool in here.

409
00:23:17,341 --> 00:23:21,674
Let's shop and relax a bit.

410
00:23:21,697 --> 00:23:23,197
Scene 9: Delicious Eats at Tsukiji Outer Market

411
00:23:23,197 --> 00:23:27,947
We've arrived at Tsukiji Outer Market.

412
00:23:27,971 --> 00:23:31,406
It's packed already, even this early.

413
00:23:31,430 --> 00:23:35,774
That's because there's so much delicious food here!

414
00:23:35,797 --> 00:23:39,180
Mmm, something smells amazing.

415
00:23:39,203 --> 00:23:43,395
They're selling tamagoyaki over there.

416
00:23:43,419 --> 00:23:46,319
I’d love to try one.

417
00:23:46,342 --> 00:23:48,724
I'll buy one.

418
00:23:48,748 --> 00:23:51,651
Careful, it's hot!

419
00:23:51,674 --> 00:23:54,013
Be careful.

420
00:23:54,037 --> 00:23:57,670
It's sweet and so tasty!

421
00:23:57,693 --> 00:24:01,264
Should we try a seafood bowl too?

422
00:24:01,288 --> 00:24:03,606
Yes, it is.

423
00:24:03,629 --> 00:24:06,896
Let's go to that restaurant over there.

424
00:24:06,919 --> 00:24:10,019
Sorry about that.

425
00:24:10,042 --> 00:24:13,675
Two seafood bowls, please.

426
00:24:13,698 --> 00:24:18,615
Oh, I can't eat wasabi.

427
00:24:18,639 --> 00:24:22,239
I'll let them know.

428
00:24:22,262 --> 00:24:26,129
Please don't add wasabi to one of them.

429
00:24:26,152 --> 00:24:28,385
Thanks a lot!

430
00:24:28,408 --> 00:24:31,108
Here it comes!

431
00:24:31,131 --> 00:24:34,327
The fish looks so fresh!

432
00:24:34,350 --> 00:24:37,737
This is absolutely delicious!

433
00:24:37,761 --> 00:24:41,502
I'm so full!

434
00:24:41,525 --> 00:24:44,359
Let's walk to Ginza.

435
00:24:44,382 --> 00:24:48,135
What kind of place is Ginza?

436
00:24:48,158 --> 00:24:52,391
It's right next to Tsukiji.

437
00:24:52,414 --> 00:24:56,285
It's a beautiful and upscale town.

438
00:24:56,309 --> 00:25:00,484
There are so many big department stores here.

439
00:25:00,507 --> 00:25:04,374
Let's check out some famous shops.

440
00:25:04,397 --> 00:25:08,742
Wow, what a gorgeous bag!

441
00:25:08,766 --> 00:25:11,350
That sounds nice!

442
00:25:11,373 --> 00:25:13,840
How much is it?

443
00:25:13,863 --> 00:25:18,330
Uh, it's 300,000 yen.

444
00:25:18,353 --> 00:25:21,928
300,000 yen?

445
00:25:21,951 --> 00:25:25,268
That's really expensive.

446
00:25:25,291 --> 00:25:27,428
Yes, it is.

447
00:25:27,451 --> 00:25:30,050
I'll just look for now.

448
00:25:30,073 --> 00:25:32,230
Good idea.

449
00:25:32,254 --> 00:25:36,487
Let's walk along the street outside.

450
00:25:36,510 --> 00:25:39,577
It's a pedestrian paradise!

451
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:42,586
There are no cars around.

452
00:25:42,610 --> 00:25:46,876
We can walk right down the middle of the road.

453
00:25:46,899 --> 00:25:49,655
This is so fun!

454
00:25:49,679 --> 00:25:52,584
Let's take a photo.

455
00:26:02,616 --> 00:26:04,116
Scene 10: Tokyo Station and the Imperial Palace

456
00:26:04,116 --> 00:26:08,272
This is Tokyo Station.

457
00:26:08,295 --> 00:26:12,962
Wow, what a stunning red building!

458
00:26:12,985 --> 00:26:16,544
That's the Marunouchi Station Building.

459
00:26:16,568 --> 00:26:19,268
It's an old building.

460
00:26:19,291 --> 00:26:22,485
It has so much history.

461
00:26:22,508 --> 00:26:27,213
If you walk straight ahead, you'll reach the Imperial Palace.

462
00:26:27,237 --> 00:26:30,182
What's the Imperial Palace?

463
00:26:30,205 --> 00:26:34,744
It's where the Emperor of Japan resides.

464
00:26:34,767 --> 00:26:37,443
That's incredible!

465
00:26:37,467 --> 00:26:39,584
Let's go!

466
00:26:39,608 --> 00:26:43,241
This is a huge plaza.

467
00:26:43,264 --> 00:26:46,597
There are so many pine trees.

468
00:26:46,620 --> 00:26:50,001
There's a bridge over there.

469
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:53,221
That's the Nijubashi Bridge.

470
00:26:53,244 --> 00:26:56,077
It's very famous.

471
00:26:56,100 --> 00:26:59,267
Let's take a photo.

472
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:03,357
Now, let's head back to Tokyo Station.

473
00:27:03,380 --> 00:27:06,446
Let's go underground.

474
00:27:06,469 --> 00:27:09,636
What's down here?

475
00:27:09,659 --> 00:27:13,893
There are lots of souvenir shops.

476
00:27:13,916 --> 00:27:18,053
I'd like to buy some souvenirs for my family.

477
00:27:18,076 --> 00:27:23,195
This is Tokyo Station Ichibangai.

478
00:27:23,219 --> 00:27:28,285
There are so many shops—I might get lost!

479
00:27:28,308 --> 00:27:31,542
Be careful, okay?

480
00:27:31,565 --> 00:27:36,898
Oh, there's the most popular snack!

481
00:27:36,921 --> 00:27:39,797
That's Tokyo Banana, right?

482
00:27:39,820 --> 00:27:42,687
It's delicious!

483
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:46,047
I'll take three of those.

484
00:27:46,070 --> 00:27:50,937
That wraps up our Tokyo sightseeing.

485
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:54,194
We walked a lot today, didn't we?

486
00:27:54,217 --> 00:27:57,173
Are you tired?

487
00:27:57,197 --> 00:28:00,497
A little.

488
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:04,234
But I had so much fun!

489
00:28:04,258 --> 00:28:07,647
I'm glad to hear that.

490
00:28:07,670 --> 00:28:12,537
Asakusa and Shinjuku were both so interesting.

491
00:28:12,560 --> 00:28:17,260
Which area did you like the most?

492
00:28:17,283 --> 00:28:21,516
Akihabara was my favorite.

493
00:28:21,539 --> 00:28:23,606
Really?

494
00:28:23,629 --> 00:28:28,529
Please come visit Japan again!

495
00:28:28,552 --> 00:28:32,118
Yes, I definitely will!

496
00:28:32,142 --> 00:28:35,052
Thank you so much!